==Battleground==
*4 [[Heavenly Hippoe]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 33.33~40 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,200f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
*1 [[Camelle]] spawns as the boss after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Hippoe]]s spawn after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 23.33~26.67 seconds<sup>700f~800f</sup>.
*8 [[Hyppoh]]s spawn after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 16.67~20 seconds<sup>500f~600f</sup>.
*1 [[Heavenly Hippoe]] spawns after 120 seconds<sup>3,600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Arguably easier than [[3rd Round: Dawn (Insane)]], as the Angelic Gories are removed and the support is weaker in general. To balance this out, Camelle is no longer on base hit, and spawns after a mere 13.33 seconds. Make sure your [[:Category:Meatshield-class Cats|meatshields]] are strong enough to survive at least one hit from Camelle, or else Camelle will be pushing constantly and you will die. The Hyppohs and Heavenly Hippoes are fairly weak, but the Heavenly Hippoes can chip down your meatshields slowly if you let them stack, so if you are able to save up for him, [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]] can help if the Hyppohs and Heavenly Hippoes are blocking Camelle from hitting him. If you do not have a lot of [[Anti-unstarred Alien Treasures]], get some, as they will help with the Hyppohs if you are struggling here.

